# Known divergence (by design): this DefineIndex() ACL security test defines
# public.setter() with a SET search_path in its body (a probe that the planner-
# time search_path change stays isolated). That SET is untrackable session state,
# so the gateway rejects setter's CREATE; s.const() then references the missing
# setter and fails at the backend with "function does not exist", aborting the
# transaction, so the remaining setup reports "current transaction is aborted"
# and the final expected error shifts from 42704 (undefined collation) to 25P02
# (in_failed_transaction). setter cannot be pre-seeded — running its SET through
# the pooler is the exact session-state leak the feature prevents. The property
# under test is PostgreSQL backend behavior, covered by PostgreSQL's own suite.
